{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014yTVZvY1Mu9ayyFCcBeEKu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — SOS 4: Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n4\t\n5\t### TestTogetherAsOneProperties (4 tests)\n6\tValidates static card metadata matches the card spec:\n7\t- `test_is_sorcery` — Card is a Sorcery subclass.\n8\t- `test_name` — Name is \"Together as One\".\n9\t- `test_mana_cost` — Mana cost is `{6}`.\n10\t- `test_has_sorcery_card_type` — CardType.SORCERY is in card_types.\n11\t\n12\t### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting (5 tests)\n13\tThe card specifies \"target player\" (for drawing) and \"any target\" (for damage). This requires two TargetRequirements.\n14\t- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — get_targets() returns exactly 2 items.\n15\t- `test_each_requirement_is_target_requirement` — Both are TargetRequirement instances.\n16\t- `test_first_target_accepts_player` — The player-draw target accepts a player object.\n17\t- `test_second_target_accepts_player` — \"Any target\" accepts a player.\n18\t- `test_second_target_accepts_creature` — \"Any target\" accepts a creature.\n19\t\n20\t### TestTogetherAsOneConverge (1 test)\n21\tThe Converge mechanic relies on a `colors_spent` attribute (per FDN 205 pattern).\n22\t- `test_colors_spent_attribute_exists` — Card has a colors_spent attribute.\n23\t\n24\t### TestTogetherAsOneDrawCards (2 tests)\n25\tValidates the \"target player draws X cards\" effect.\n26\t- `test_target_player_draws_x_cards` — With 3 colors spent and target = opponent, opponent draws 3.\n27\t- `test_caster_can_target_self_for_draw` — Caster can target themselves for draws.\n28\t\n29\t### TestTogetherAsOneDamage (3 tests)\n30\tValidates the \"deals X damage to any target\" effect.\n31\t- `test_deals_x_damage_to_target_player` — Deals 3 damage to a player with 3 colors.\n32\t- `test_deals_x_damage_to_creature` — Deals 2 damage to a creature with 2 colors.\n33\t- `test_five_colors_deals_five_damage` — Full WUBRG deals 5 damage.\n34\t\n35\t### TestTogetherAsOneLifeGain (2 tests)\n36\tValidates the \"you gain X life\" effect.\n37\t- `test_controller_gains_x_life` — Controller gains 3 life with 3 colors.\n38\t- `test_five_colors_gains_five_life` — Controller gains 5 life with 5 colors.\n39\t\n40\t### TestTogetherAsOneFullResolution (1 test)\n41\tValidates all three effects occur together in a single resolution.\n42\t- `test_all_three_effects_with_three_colors` — Draw 3, deal 3 damage to creature, gain 3 life all in one call.\n43\t\n44\t### TestTogetherAsOneZeroColors (3 tests)\n45\tEdge case: X = 0 means all effects are zero.\n46\t- `test_zero_colors_no_cards_drawn` — No cards drawn when X = 0.\n47\t- `test_zero_colors_no_damage` — No damage dealt when X = 0.\n48\t- `test_zero_colors_no_life_gain` — No life gained when X = 0.\n49\t\n50\t### TestTogetherAsOneNoTargets (2 tests)\n51\tEdge case: missing or empty chosen_targets should not crash.\n52\t- `test_no_chosen_targets_does_not_raise` — No chosen_targets attribute set.\n53\t- `test_empty_chosen_targets_does_not_raise` — Empty list for chosen_targets.\n54\t\n55\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeWithColorList (2 tests)\n56\tThe engine casting pipeline sets `colors_spent` as a list of Color enum objects. The card must handle both int (test convenience) and list (engine reality) formats.\n57\t- `test_colors_spent_as_list_determines_x` — List of 3 Color enums means X = 3.\n58\t- `test_colors_spent_as_list_gains_life` — Life gain correct with list-format colors_spent.\n59\t\n60\t## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n61\t- **Countered spell**: The card going to graveyard after being countered is engine behavior, not card-specific.\n62\t- **Protection from the spell**: Protection preventing damage is engine-level behavior tested in engine_tests.\n63\t- **Drawing from empty library**: The draw-from-empty-library SBA is engine behavior, not specific to this card.\n64\t- **Multiple casts of the same card**: No unique per-card state that would differ on re-cast beyond colors_spent, which is reset by the engine.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0197ndBubDQvNnasBuqjywDt","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"96152cdb-f96d-40ff-aa42-090ce79429fc","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:26:49.488Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_4"}
