{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VnjjP4bYfmd7Lyive6ujPr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_4 (Together as One)\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t1. **Sorcery base class**: Extended `Sorcery` from `engine.card` since this is a sorcery spell. The `Sorcery.__init__` automatically adds `CardType.SORCERY` to `card_types`.\n6\t\n7\t2. **Converge via `colors_spent` attribute**: Following the FDN 205 (Wardens of the Cycle) pattern, the card tracks `colors_spent` as an attribute. Default is `0` (int). The `_get_x()` helper handles both int and list-of-Color-enum formats -- the engine casting pipeline may set it as a list of `Color` enums, while tests set it directly as an int.\n8\t\n9\t3. **Two TargetRequirements**: `get_targets()` returns exactly two `TargetRequirement` objects:\n10\t   - First: \"target player\" -- filters on `hasattr(obj, \"life\")` (the standard player detection pattern).\n11\t   - Second: \"any target\" -- accepts players (have `life`) and creatures/planeswalkers (have `card_types` containing CREATURE or PLANESWALKER).\n12\t\n13\t4. **Resolution order**: `on_resolve()` follows oracle text order: draw X cards for target player, deal X damage to any target, controller gains X life. Uses `engine.game.draw_card` and `engine.game.deal_damage` for correct event firing.\n14\t\n15\t5. **Edge case handling**: Gracefully handles missing/empty `chosen_targets` (no crash), zero colors spent (all effects are no-ops), and self-targeting (caster can target themselves for draw).\n16\t\n17\t## Conventions\n18\t\n19\t- `kwargs.setdefault()` pattern for card properties, consistent with FDN 205.\n20\t- `colors_spent` attribute initialized in `__init__`, set externally by cast logic or test code.\n21\t- No engine modifications were needed.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YK3sAhTenQdHp7jtu2hapu","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"094e9eb0-ce82-444c-855f-4bfae613eda1","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:27:24.200Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_4 implementation"}
