{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019QdEExkjXGdrRXc7GUsdiQ","type":"tool_result","content":"140-719. Case Cards\n141-720. Omen Cards\n142-721. Station Cards\n143:722. Preparation Cards\n144-723. Controlling Another Player\n145-724. Ending Turns and Phases\n146-725. The Monarch\n--\n6097-\n6098-721.4. Any ability a station card has that isn’t preceded by a station symbol is treated normally. In particular, each station card has its station ability (see rule 702.184) at all times. That ability may be activated regardless of how many charge counters are on it.\n6099-\n6100:722. Preparation Cards\n6101-\n6102:722.1. Preparation cards have a two-part card frame, with a smaller frame inset within their text box.\n6103-\n6104:722.2. The text that appears in the inset frame on the right defines alternative characteristics that the object may have while it’s a spell. The card’s normal characteristics appear as usual, although with a smaller text box on the left.\n6105-\n6106:722.2a The inset frame of a preparation card is called a “prepare spell.” If a rule or effect refers to a card, spell, or permanent that has a prepare spell, it refers to an object for which these alternative characteristics exist, even if the object currently doesn’t use them.\n6107-\n6108:722.2b The existence and values of these alternative characteristics are part of the object’s copiable values.\n6109-\n6110:722.2c Although preparation cards are printed with multiple sets of characteristics, each preparation card is only one card. For example, a player who has drawn or discarded a preparation card has drawn or discarded one card, not two.\n6111-\n6112:722.3. Preparation cards can’t be cast using the alternative characteristics found within their inset frames. Rather, these characteristics are used to define characteristics of copies which may be cast.\n6113-\n6114:[Omitted long matching line]\n6115-\n6116:722.3b A rule or effect may cause a permanent to become “unprepared.” This removes the prepared designation from that permanent.\n6117-\n6118:[Omitted long matching line]\n6119-[Omitted long context line]\n6120-\n6121:722.3d If a prepare spell is copied, the copy is also a prepare spell. Any rule or effect that refers to a spell cast as a prepare spell refers to the copy as well.\n6122-\n6123:722.4. In every zone, a preparation card has only its normal characteristics.\n6124-\n6125:722.5. If an effect instructs a player to choose a card name and the player wants to choose a preparation card’s alternative name, the player may do so.\n6126-\n6127-723. Controlling Another Player\n6128-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoVxZ1e52LkijbBSBoV3DU","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"9ffbdcf2-17e9-4b49-b71c-5b7b2b132fbe","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:31:24.338Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_13"}
