{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EUQ8rrQriUu5Z5AnnMZeru","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011sW48ixw9VQxGCxcHUb6MC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale for sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Class Hierarchy\n- Extends `Creature` since the front face is a 3/3 creature. The card name is set to \"Emeritus of Truce\" (the front face name only), matching the test expectation.\n\n### ETB Trigger\n- Registers an `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger via `register_triggers()`, with a condition that checks `event.permanent is source` to ensure it only triggers on self-entry.\n- The trigger effect delegates to `on_resolve()` so the same token-creation and prepared-check logic is used whether the trigger fires naturally or the test calls `on_resolve()` directly.\n\n### Targeting\n- `get_targets()` returns a single `TargetRequirement` with a `filter_fn` that accepts any `Player` instance. This supports targeting both self and opponents for the token creation.\n\n### Token Creation\n- Uses `engine.game.create_token()` to create a 1/1 Inkling creature token with flying under the target player's control.\n- Token has `subtypes={\"Inkling\"}`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING`, and `colors=[\"W\", \"B\"]` for white and black.\n\n### Prepared Condition\n- After token creation, iterates over all players that are not the controller. If any opponent controls more creatures than the controller, sets `self.is_prepared = True`.\n- Creature counting uses `CardType.CREATURE in card_types` check on all objects on each player's battlefield.\n- The `is_prepared` flag defaults to `False` in `__init__` and is only set to `True` when the condition is met.\n\n### Edge Cases\n- `on_resolve()` gracefully handles missing or empty `chosen_targets` by returning early (no-op).\n- The prepared check correctly handles equal counts (not prepared) and strictly-more cases.\n\n## No Engine Modifications\nNo engine files were modified. The existing engine API (triggers, events, token creation, zones) was sufficient.\n\n## Conventions\n- Player detection uses `isinstance(obj, Player)` from `engine.player`.\n- Token colors are set as a list attribute `colors = [\"W\", \"B\"]` on the token object.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":53113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":146,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmsndJiRpYV9ifKJBLLPN6","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"8cd8fc5b-4ff9-4601-9ffe-63bced0759b1","request_id":"req_011CbUjtdytTnxNdRYT7Kp2z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13"}
