{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4mAJw5ETbx2Mq1u9xZv8s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'prepared' designation and the ability to cast a copy of the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares) require engine infrastructure that does not exist yet. There is no engine API for prepared/unprepared designations, nor for creating a copy of the prepare spell in exile. The implementer will need to add this to the engine or the card implementation.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"Engine support for the 'prepared' designation on permanents, plus a mechanism to create a copy of the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares instant) in exile that can be cast. This could be a simple boolean flag (is_prepared) plus a method that creates the spell copy and handles the unprepare on cast.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"1/1 white and black Inkling creature token\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The 'white and black' color attribute of the token cannot be fully asserted because the engine's Creature class does not have a standard 'colors' field for verifying multi-color identity. We test name/subtype ('Inkling'), power/toughness (1/1), and flying keyword, but cannot assert the token's color identity is exactly {W, B}.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A 'colors' attribute on Creature/CardImpl (e.g. a set of Color enums) that the implementer sets when creating the token, which tests can then inspect.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RSxdPURqSEmkgi1J5XTBqG","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"e380705d-68e0-466e-b521-2732c0059995","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:37:38.067Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13 implementation"}
