{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUp8U6c1euvtbUJVD5wKak","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_57\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The exact timing of 'at the beginning of your next main phase' requires a full turn-cycle simulation with phase transitions, delayed trigger firing at specific phase boundaries, and verification that the trigger fires on the correct player's main phase (not opponent's). The delayed trigger registration and its effect (adding the correct amount of colorless mana) are tested, but the precise timing integration with the turn system is not covered.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A test helper like advance_to_next_main_phase(game, player_index) that simulates the turn advancing until the specified player's next main phase, firing all delayed triggers at the correct time, would allow full integration testing of the timing.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_57\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The oracle text says 'mana spent to cast that spell', which for X spells or spells with additional costs could differ from the printed mana cost's CMC. The engine does not currently track the actual total mana spent to cast a specific spell as a separate attribute on the card/stack object. Tests use mana_cost.cmc as a proxy. For non-X, non-additional-cost spells this is correct.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An attribute like stack_obj.total_mana_spent or card.mana_spent_to_cast that the casting pipeline sets to the actual total mana paid would allow testing the exact 'mana spent' semantics for X spells and spells with additional costs.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"