{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016kFwMy3kMQXDhEHLfVqq45","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\nfiles_changed: 2 (cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py, engine/events.py)\ntests_passing: all (26/26 card tests, 1145/1145 engine tests)\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised-rationale.md\nnotes: Fixed both strict review comments: (1) replaced overly broad TriggeredEvent with new BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent and added player-checking condition, (2) added self-unregistration via game.trigger_manager.unregister(source) inside the effect closure to make the delayed trigger one-shot."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: addb9316dfbcfb6cf (use SendMessage with to: 'addb9316dfbcfb6cf' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 37520\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 99026</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"9b13e316-7a6c-49ea-8650-beba978ffd0b","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:47:07.817Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"\n## Task\nRevise **sos_57** to address two strict review comments. You MUST NOT modify any test file.\n\n## Strict comments to address\n\n### 1. Overly broad delayed trigger (line ~97)\nThe delayed trigger is registered with event_type=TriggeredEvent (base class) and condition=None, which means it fires on ANY event. It should use a more specific event type or at minimum have a condition restricting when it fires. For \"at the beginning of your next main phase\", consider using BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent or similar, with a condition checking the controller is the active player.\n\n### 2. Trigger never unregistered (line ~97)\nDelayed triggers in MTG are one-shot. This trigger will fire on every event indefinitely. The effect should unregister itself after firing once.\n\n## What to do\n1. Read current: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`\n2. Read tests: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n3. Read engine triggers: `/workspace/engine/triggers.py`, `/workspace/engine/events.py`\n4. Fix: Make the delayed trigger more specific and self-removing, while still passing all tests.\n5. Read the review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json`\n\n## Verification\nRun: `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py -v --tb=short`\nRun: `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ --tb=short -q`\n\n## Output\n1. Rationale → `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised-rationale.md`\n2. Disagreements → `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/disagreements.json`\n\nReturn REVISION_DONE with disagreement_count.\n","agentId":"addb9316dfbcfb6cf","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"REVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\nfiles_changed: 2 (cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py, engine/events.py)\ntests_passing: all (26/26 card tests, 1145/1145 engine tests)\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised-rationale.md\nnotes: Fixed both strict review comments: (1) replaced overly broad TriggeredEvent with new BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent and added player-checking condition, (2) added self-unregistration via game.trigger_manager.unregister(source) inside the effect closure to make the delayed trigger one-shot."}],"totalDurationMs":99026,"totalTokens":37520,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":37057,"output_tokens":195,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":267},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":195,"cache_read_input_tokens":37057,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":267,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"t