{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nm7B7uR8fRK6Z4XFeZmE3U","type":"tool_result","content":"3500\tExample: Darksteel Colossus and Gravebane Zombie are put into a player’s graveyard from the battlefield at the same time. Darksteel Colossus says in part “If Darksteel Colossus would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Darksteel Colossus and shuffle it into its owner’s library instead.” Gravebane Zombie says “If this creature would die, put it on top of its owner’s library instead.” The player shuffles Darksteel Colossus into their library and puts Gravebane Zombie on top of that library.\n3501\t\n3502\t701.25. Surveil\n3503\t\n3504\t701.25a To “surveil N” means to look at the top N cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.\n3505\t\n3506\t701.25b If an effect allows you to look at additional cards while you surveil, those cards are included among the cards you may put into your graveyard and on top of your library in any order.\n3507\t\n3508\t701.25c If a player is instructed to surveil 0, no surveil event occurs. Abilities that trigger whenever a player surveils won’t trigger.\n3509\t\n3510\t701.25d An ability that triggers whenever a player surveils triggers after the process described in rule 701.25a is complete, even if some or all of those actions were impossible.\n3511\t\n3512\t701.26. Tap and Untap\n3513\t\n3514\t701.26a To tap a permanent, turn it sideways from an upright position. Only untapped permanents can be tapped.\n3515\t\n3516\t701.26b To untap a permanent, rotate it back to the upright position from a sideways position. Only tapped permanents can be untapped.\n3517\t\n3518\t701.27. Transform\n3519\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PXaXZnxyVjH8ZnnttBcNNj","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"38330fc3-72b2-4342-98ef-0a73f6aae733","timestamp":"2026-05-28T09:48:21.964Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
