{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SMRxfroF7SEntL3FEAX95q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HNnf4zBgt5hL4kNYD51h34","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale for SOS 97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n\n### TestRalZarekProperties (8 tests)\nValidates all static card properties from the card spec.\n\n- **test_is_planeswalker**: Card must be an instance of the Planeswalker base class.\n- **test_name**: Card name must be \"Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer\".\n- **test_mana_cost**: Mana cost must be {1}{B}{B}.\n- **test_starting_loyalty**: Starting loyalty must be 3.\n- **test_initial_loyalty_equals_starting**: loyalty attribute should start equal to starting_loyalty.\n- **test_is_legendary**: Must have Supertype.LEGENDARY.\n- **test_has_ral_subtype**: Must have \"Ral\" in subtypes.\n- **test_has_planeswalker_card_type**: Must have CardType.PLANESWALKER.\n\n### TestRalZarekLoyaltyAbilities (3 tests)\nValidates the structure of loyalty abilities returned by get_loyalty_abilities().\n\n- **test_returns_four_abilities**: Must return exactly 4 abilities (+1, -1, -2, -7).\n- **test_all_are_loyalty_abilities**: Each returned object must be a LoyaltyAbility instance.\n- **test_loyalty_costs_are_correct**: Costs must be [1, -1, -2, -7] in order.\n\n### TestRalZarekSurveil (3 tests)\nValidates the +1 loyalty ability: Surveil 2.\n\n- **test_surveil_moves_cards_from_library**: Surveil 2 should look at top 2 cards and redistribute them between library top and graveyard. Card counts must remain consistent.\n- **test_surveil_with_fewer_than_two_cards_in_library**: Edge case: library has only 1 card. Should surveil that 1 card without crashing.\n- **test_surveil_with_empty_library**: Edge case: empty library. Should be a no-op per rules (surveil 0-ish).\n\n### TestRalZarekDiscard (3 tests)\nValidates the -1 loyalty ability: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n\n- **test_discard_single_player**: Targeting one player causes that player to discard 1 card.\n- **test_discard_both_players**: Targeting both players causes each to discard 1 card.\n- **test_discard_player_with_empty_hand**: Edge case: targeting a player with no cards in hand should not crash.\n\n### TestRalZarekReanimate (8 tests)\nValidates the -2 loyalty ability: Return target creature with MV <= 3 from graveyard to battlefield.\n\n- **test_returns_creature_to_battlefield**: A creature with MV <= 3 in the graveyard should be moved to the battlefield.\n- **test_returns_creature_with_mv_exactly_three**: MV 3 is the upper bound and should be valid.\n- **test_returns_creature_with_mv_zero**: MV 0 should be valid (edge case).\n- **test_get_targets_returns_graveyard_requirement**: get_targets should advertise a graveyard-zone target requirement.\n- **test_target_filter_accepts_creature_mv_le_3**: Filter should accept creatures with MV <= 3.\n- **test_target_filter_rejects_creature_mv_gt_3**: Filter should reject creatures with MV > 3.\n- **test_target_filter_rejects_non_creature**: Filter should reject non-creature cards regardless of MV.\n- **test_reanimate_empty_graveyard_no_crash**: Edge case: no valid target should be safe.\n\n### TestRalZarekUltimate (3 tests)\nValidates the -7 loyalty ability: Flip five coins, target opponent skips X turns.\n\n- **test_ultimate_loyalty_cost**: The ability must have loyalty cost -7.\n- **test_ultimate_skips_opponent_turns**: After resolution, some turn-skipping mechanism should be applied to the opponent.\n- **test_ultimate_with_no_heads_skips_zero_turns**: Edge case: 0 heads should cause 0 turns skipped and not crash.\n\n### Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **Specific surveil card ordering**: Surveil lets the player choose which cards to put on top or in graveyard. The simplified engine uses deterministic behavior (likely puts all into graveyard). Testing exact ordering would require scripted player choices, which is covered by the consistency check.\n- **Coin flip randomness seeding**: The exact mechanism for coin flips is implementation-dependent. Tests check observable state changes rather than the specific randomization method.\n- **Planeswalker loyalty adjustment on activation**: This is an engine-level concern (the engine should add/subtract loyalty when activating a loyalty ability), not a card-level behavior.\n- **Legendary rule (only one Ral on the battlefield)**: This is an engine state-based action, not a card implementation detail.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6151,"cache_read_input_tokens":69200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6151,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PXaXZnxyVjH8ZnnttBcNNj","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"792e6d77-e637-4445-a7ac-465438d90b43","request_id":"req_011CbUkweky5JAx2xXeYDC25","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_97"}
