{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HSC5KdshSD9bu9s3Gawmpx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015f2KMvP133wLR4R4LY1khX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 145,\n    \"comment\": \"The -2 reanimate ability uses `engine.zones.move_zone` (the low-level zone transition) instead of `engine.zones.move_to_zone` (the high-level one). `move_zone` only moves the object between ZoneContainer instances without firing EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent, registering triggers/replacement effects, or consulting replacement effects. When a creature is returned to the battlefield, it should trigger ETB events and get its abilities registered. Use `from engine.zones import move_to_zone` and call `move_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)` instead. This matches the pattern used by other engine functions like `create_token`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, etc.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 66,\n    \"comment\": \"The `get_targets` method always returns the -2 ability's TargetRequirement (graveyard creature with MV<=3), regardless of which loyalty ability is being activated. The -1 ability (targeting any number of players) and -7 ability (targeting an opponent) have no corresponding TargetRequirement definitions. While this is consistent with how other planeswalkers in the codebase handle targeting (via _resolve_targets/chosen_targets attributes set externally), it means the engine's targeting validation cannot be used for those abilities. If the engine ever enforces targeting via get_targets, these abilities would break.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 104,\n    \"comment\": \"The surveil implementation always puts all surveiled cards into the graveyard. Per the Oracle text, surveil lets the controller choose which cards go to the graveyard and which stay on top of the library. The comment acknowledges this is a 'simplified surveil' which is acceptable, but worth noting for completeness.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 175,\n    \"comment\": \"The `skip_turns` attribute is dynamically added to a Player object (`target.skip_turns`). There is no engine-level support for turn-skipping using this counter, so this is purely a data marker that tests can check. If the engine's turn loop doesn't consult `player.skip_turns`, the ultimate's effect is effectively a no-op in real gameplay. This is consistent with the test expectations but worth documenting.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":509,"cache_read_input_tokens":40358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":509,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GrmWnu9DHQeBxsFqSJEsVC","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"8381148e-d7d3-4f74-8932-93938485ca31","request_id":"req_011CbUmL8H41B2UTtN6xgvVG","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
