{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Wz1bnSiBQERSCRUMkjffYi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016tnwfWhtyrC8nEEDf2Nw7g","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# Revision Rationale for sos_97\n\n## Change Made\n\nReplaced the low-level `move_zone` call with the high-level `move_to_zone` call in the `-2` reanimate ability.\n\n### Before\n```python\nfrom engine.zones import move_zone\nbattlefield = game.get_battlefield(controller)\nmove_zone(target, graveyard, battlefield)\n```\n\n### After\n```python\nfrom engine.zones import move_to_zone\nmove_to_zone(game, target, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n```\n\n## Why\n\n`move_zone` is a low-level zone transition that only physically moves objects between ZoneContainers. It does not fire ETB events, register triggers, or process replacement effects.\n\n`move_to_zone` is the high-level API that:\n1. Fires `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` when entering the battlefield\n2. Registers triggers and replacement effects for the entering permanent\n3. Handles leaving-battlefield hooks if applicable\n4. Consults replacement effects for zone-change redirection\n\nSince the -2 ability returns a creature to the battlefield, it should use the high-level API so that any ETB triggers on the reanimated creature fire correctly.\n\n## No other changes needed\n\nAll 28 card tests and all 1145 engine tests pass with this change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":159,"cache_read_input_tokens":30093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":159,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XT1rPHAvAWPtR7g7nJVFmE","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0