{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01P2XvapVnMym7Ma3e9jr7ny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153GqvZyksqDioLxg8jeme8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale: SOS 120 -- Improvisation Capstone\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties (7 tests)\n\nStatic property tests verifying the card matches its spec:\n\n- **test_is_sorcery** -- Card must be a Sorcery subclass (type_line: \"Sorcery -- Lesson\").\n- **test_name** -- Card name must be \"Improvisation Capstone\".\n- **test_mana_cost** -- Mana cost must parse as {5}{R}{R}.\n- **test_has_sorcery_card_type** -- CardType.SORCERY must be present.\n- **test_has_lesson_subtype** -- \"Lesson\" must be in subtypes (spell subtype from type_line).\n- **test_mana_value_is_seven** -- CMC should be 7 (5 generic + 2 red).\n- **test_color_is_red** -- Red pips must be present in mana cost.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneExileFromLibrary (4 tests)\n\nTests the primary ability: \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total mana value 4 or greater.\"\n\n- **test_exiles_cards_until_total_mv_four_or_greater** -- Verifies that cards are exiled one-by-one from library top and the process stops once cumulative MV >= 4.\n- **test_single_card_with_mv_four_stops_immediately** -- If the first card has MV >= 4, exactly one card is exiled.\n- **test_multiple_small_cards_exiled_until_threshold** -- With all MV-1 cards, exactly 4 should be exiled.\n- **test_cards_are_exiled_not_put_elsewhere** -- Exiled library cards should be in the exile zone, not graveyard.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneFreeCast (2 tests)\n\nTests: \"You may cast any number of spells from among them without paying their mana costs.\"\n\n- **test_exiled_spells_are_castable_for_free** -- Spells resolve even with empty mana pool.\n- **test_creature_among_exiled_cards_can_be_cast** -- Creatures (permanents) among exiled cards should be castable and end up on the battlefield.\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmExile (2 tests)\n\nTests the first part of Paradigm: \"Then exile this spell.\"\n\n- **test_spell_is_exiled_after_resolution** -- The capstone itself should be in exile after resolution.\n- **test_spell_not_in_graveyard_after_resolution** -- Must NOT be in graveyard (Paradigm replaces normal sorcery graveyard placement).\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneParadigmRecurrence (4 tests)\n\nTests the recurring paradigm trigger: \"After you first resolve a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.\"\n\n- **test_paradigm_registers_delayed_trigger_after_first_resolution** -- A trigger must be registered after first resolution.\n- **test_paradigm_trigger_fires_at_main_phase** -- The trigger fires on BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent for the controller.\n- **test_paradigm_trigger_does_not_fire_for_opponent** -- Should not fire on the opponent's main phase.\n- **test_paradigm_creates_copy_in_exile** -- When the trigger resolves, a copy is created (in exile or on the stack).\n\n### TestImprovisationCapstoneEdgeCases (4 tests)\n\n- **test_empty_library_does_not_crash** -- Gracefully handle empty library.\n- **test_library_with_insufficient_total_mv** -- If entire library totals < 4 MV, all cards are exiled.\n- **test_zero_mv_cards_are_counted** -- Zero-MV cards contribute 0 but are still exiled, and the process continues.\n- **test_on_resolve_with_no_castable_spells** -- Lands (not castable) among exiled cards should not crash resolution.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **\"You may\" choice**: The oracle says \"you may cast\", implying a choice. Testing the opt-out path (choosing not to cast) would require scripting DeterministicPlayer choices in a complex interaction that depends on implementation details. Covered indirectly by the lands test.\n- **Paradigm \"first resolve\" tracking across multiple instances**: Testing that a second physical copy skips the paradigm setup is deferred since it requires multiple instances in a game -- complex multi-card interaction beyond core requirements.\n- **Interaction with other paradigm cards**: Out of scope for this single card's tests.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6116,"cache_read_input_tokens":65114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6116,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCBW6ooPfaYqp7MLVWKPD3","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"323a2f74-ea8c-4eb1-8ac9-d6a009b8f190","request_id":"req_011CbUmfyAvG9eo5odMjopEx","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_120"}
