{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01URRbACkG2nkbuP21hjdgzf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale: sos_120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Card Structure\n6\t- Extends `Sorcery` base class with Lesson subtype, matching the card spec.\n7\t- Mana cost `{5}{R}{R}` (CMC 7) set via `ManaCost.parse`.\n8\t\n9\t### Main Effect: Exile from Library\n10\t- Iterates from the top of the library, removing and exiling cards one at a time.\n11\t- Tracks running total of mana values; stops when total >= 4 or library is empty.\n12\t- Cards with no `mana_cost` attribute contribute 0 to the total.\n13\t\n14\t### Free-Cast from Exile\n15\t- Key design: exiled cards remain in exile after `on_resolve` completes. StackObjects are pushed for each castable spell, and their `on_resolve` callbacks handle moving the card from exile to its destination (battlefield for creatures, graveyard for instants/sorceries).\n16\t- This deferred approach is necessary because tests check the exile zone immediately after `on_resolve` (before stack resolution) and expect the exiled library cards to still be present.\n17\t- Lands are skipped since they are not spells.\n18\t- Used closure factories (`_make_creature_resolve`, `_make_spell_resolve`) to capture card references correctly in the loop.\n19\t\n20\t### Paradigm: Self-Exile\n21\t- After the main effect, the spell itself is moved from the stack zone to exile.\n22\t- Checks both the stack zone and exile zone to avoid duplicates.\n23\t\n24\t### Paradigm: Recurring Trigger\n25\t- Registers a delayed trigger via `TriggerManager` that watches for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n26\t- Condition checks that `event.player` matches the controller.\n27\t- Effect creates a new `ImprovisationCapstone` instance (the \"copy\") and pushes it onto the stack as a StackObject with its own `on_resolve`.\n28\t\n29\t## Conventions Established\n30\t- For cards that exile from library then free-cast: keep cards in exile, push StackObjects for deferred casting.\n31\t- Paradigm pattern: self-exile + delayed trigger for `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` with controller condition check.\n32\t\n33\t## No Engine Modifications\n34\t- No engine files were modified. All behavior is implemented within the card class using existing engine APIs.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MU73m4KGvJ8ZA6DBm5Grjy","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"ec0696bc-4a7e-492a-a7f3-d7c8d562434e","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:03:54.221Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
