{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QnPzqkSWCFLahghAGCvqxL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HfVDHT2fS1ATfYBNz6Ti3p","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 221,\n    \"comment\": \"Bug: Paradigm copy causes exponential trigger accumulation. When the paradigm trigger fires, it creates a copy and calls `capstone_copy.on_resolve(g)` which runs the full `on_resolve` method -- including `_paradigm_register_recurrence`. This registers a SECOND trigger. On the next main phase, both triggers fire, each registering another trigger (now 4), then 8, 16, etc. The spec says 'you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases' -- this should be a single persistent trigger, not one that multiplies. Fix: the _copy_resolve callback should NOT call the full `on_resolve`; it should only perform the exile-from-library and free-cast steps (steps 1 and 2), skipping the paradigm self-exile and trigger registration (steps 3 and 4).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 159,\n    \"comment\": \"Bug: Non-creature permanents (enchantments, artifacts, planeswalkers) exiled from the library are incorrectly sent to the graveyard on resolution. The else-branch at line 159 treats all non-creature, non-land cards as instants/sorceries. If an enchantment or artifact is among the exiled cards, it should go to the battlefield (like creatures do), not to the graveyard. The implementation should check for permanent types (ENCHANTMENT, ARTIFACT, PLANESWALKER) and handle them like creatures (moving to battlefield on resolve).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 5,\n    \"comment\": \"Unused import: `import copy` is imported but never used in the module. The paradigm copy is created by constructing a new ImprovisationCapstone instance, not by using copy.copy().\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 122,\n    \"comment\": \"The oracle text says 'You may cast any number of spells' -- the word 'may' means the player can choose which (if any) to cast. The current implementation auto-casts all non-land spells without player choice. In a full implementation this would use player.choose or similar. Acceptable as a simplification given the engine's test-driven approach, but worth noting.\"\n  }\n]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":487,"cache_read_input_tokens":42776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":487,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MU73m4KGvJ8ZA6DBm5Grjy","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"e105615d-a813-4392-9948-ba621b3267fa","request_id":"req_011CbUn6Br5vz6mMz1vQRDqv","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
