{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XAKoziwGVdP1dsZcsSTRFR","type":"tool_result","content":"4665-\n4666-702.93a Undying is a triggered ability. “Undying” means “When this permanent is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, if it had no +1/+1 counters on it, return it to the battlefield under its owner’s control with a +1/+1 counter on it.”\n4667-\n4668:702.94. Miracle\n4669-\n4670:702.94a Miracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability. (See rule 603.11.) “Miracle [cost]” means “You may reveal this card from your hand as you draw it if it’s the first card you’ve drawn this turn. When you reveal this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.”\n4671-\n4672:702.94b If a player chooses to reveal a card using its miracle ability, they play with that card revealed until that card leaves their hand, that ability resolves, or that ability otherwise leaves the stack. (See rule 701.20a.)\n4673-\n4674-702.95. Soulbond\n4675-\n--\n8308-Minimum Deck Size\n8309-If a rule or effect states that a player’s deck must contain at least a specific number of cards, that number is the player’s minimum deck size.\n8310-\n8311:Miracle\n8312:A keyword ability that lets you cast a spell for a reduced cost if it’s the first card you draw in a turn. See rule 702.94, “Miracle.”\n8313-\n8314-Mobilize\n8315-A keyword ability that creates a number of tapped and attacking red Warrior creature tokens that are sacrificed at the beginning of the next end step. See rule 702.181, “Mobilize.”"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbRy9cm6u8x9yH3NFj1qpk","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"bd3fda61-f28c-44dd-b339-aa4e34c4c9fb","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:07:34.825Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_201"}
