{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UFKBLbzHNUNZMfmBoG7qdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjirEAxcGwzxvq8Bv1KDkw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale for sos_201: Lorehold, the Historian\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Static Properties\nStandard Creature subclass with Legendary supertype, Elder + Dragon subtypes, Flying + Haste keywords, 5/5 base stats, and {3}{R}{W} mana cost. Follows the established kwargs.setdefault pattern from other card implementations.\n\n### Miracle Granting via Hand Zone Proxy\nThe card's static ability \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}\" requires that any instant or sorcery in the controller's hand has a `miracle_cost` attribute set to `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")`.\n\nThe key challenge: tests create generic `Instant`/`Sorcery` objects and place them in the hand via `set_board_state`, then immediately check `getattr(card, \"miracle_cost\", None)`. There's no event fired between placement and check, so we need the attribute to be set during the add operation itself.\n\nSolution: A `_MiracleHandZoneProxy` class wraps the controller's hand `ZoneContainer`. It intercepts `add()` to automatically set `miracle_cost` on instants/sorceries, and intercepts `remove()` to clean up the attribute. All other attribute access delegates to the real zone via `__getattr__`. The proxy is installed in `register_triggers()` by replacing the hand zone entry in `controller.zones._zones[Zone.HAND]`.\n\nThis approach:\n- Only affects the Lorehold controller's hand (not opponents')\n- Automatically applies to cards added after registration\n- Also scans existing hand contents at registration time\n- Avoids modifying any engine files\n\n### Opponent's Upkeep Trigger\nRegistered as a `TriggerRegistration` watching `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` with a condition that checks `game.active_player is not controller`. This ensures it fires only on opponent upkeeps, not the controller's own.\n\nThe effect implements the \"you may discard, if you do draw\" looting pattern:\n1. Checks if hand is empty (still consumes the scripted choice to stay in sync)\n2. Uses `choose_yes_no` for the \"you may\" decision\n3. Auto-selects the only card when hand has one card, or uses `choose_card` for multi-card hands\n4. Calls `engine.game.discard` and `engine.game.draw_card` for proper zone management and event firing\n\n### Conventions Established\n- Hand zone proxy pattern for granting abilities to cards in hand: useful for future cards that modify properties of cards in a player's hand.\n- The proxy uses `object.__setattr__` in `__init__` to avoid triggering `__getattr__` delegation for internal state.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":107,"cache_read_input_tokens":81455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":107,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxNx53rTAeE5hJxNfLZLEC","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"56cac7ef-4b18-4a56-88da-9356c649a55e","request_id":"req_011CbUnej2hpzayoRT9z7HJJ","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201"}
