{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mi8dYuq3HAzWF8We5u2UCk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale for sos_201: Lorehold, the Historian\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Static Properties\n6\tStandard Creature subclass with Legendary supertype, Elder + Dragon subtypes, Flying + Haste keywords, 5/5 base stats, and {3}{R}{W} mana cost. Follows the established kwargs.setdefault pattern from other card implementations.\n7\t\n8\t### Miracle Granting via Hand Zone Proxy\n9\tThe card's static ability \"Each instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}\" requires that any instant or sorcery in the controller's hand has a `miracle_cost` attribute set to `ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")`.\n10\t\n11\tThe key challenge: tests create generic `Instant`/`Sorcery` objects and place them in the hand via `set_board_state`, then immediately check `getattr(card, \"miracle_cost\", None)`. There's no event fired between placement and check, so we need the attribute to be set during the add operation itself.\n12\t\n13\tSolution: A `_MiracleHandZoneProxy` class wraps the controller's hand `ZoneContainer`. It intercepts `add()` to automatically set `miracle_cost` on instants/sorceries, and intercepts `remove()` to clean up the attribute. All other attribute access delegates to the real zone via `__getattr__`. The proxy is installed in `register_triggers()` by replacing the hand zone entry in `controller.zones._zones[Zone.HAND]`.\n14\t\n15\tThis approach:\n16\t- Only affects the Lorehold controller's hand (not opponents')\n17\t- Automatically applies to cards added after registration\n18\t- Also scans existing hand contents at registration time\n19\t- Avoids modifying any engine files\n20\t\n21\t### Opponent's Upkeep Trigger\n22\tRegistered as a `TriggerRegistration` watching `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` with a condition that checks `game.active_player is not controller`. This ensures it fires only on opponent upkeeps, not the controller's own.\n23\t\n24\tThe effect implements the \"you may discard, if you do draw\" looting pattern:\n25\t1. Checks if hand is empty (still consumes the scripted choice to stay in sync)\n26\t2. Uses `choose_yes_no` for the \"you may\" decision\n27\t3. Auto-selects the only card when hand has one card, or uses `choose_card` for multi-card hands\n28\t4. Calls `engine.game.discard` and `engine.game.draw_card` for proper zone management and event firing\n29\t\n30\t### Conventions Established\n31\t- Hand zone proxy pattern for granting abilities to cards in hand: useful for future cards that modify properties of cards in a player's hand.\n32\t- The proxy uses `object.__setattr__` in `__init__` to avoid triggering `__getattr__` delegation for internal state.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PhCWgoY7pb2bTKbXnzjmdZ","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"68f6c647-a353-43f3-9495-6b05744659ab","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:13:16.843Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_201 implementation"}
