{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018n4Eh4w4LQKQnHShQjswsD","type":"tool_result","content":"4295-\n4296-702.39b If a creature has multiple instances of provoke, each triggers separately.\n4297-\n4298:702.40. Storm\n4299-\n4300:702.40a Storm is a triggered ability that functions on the stack. “Storm” means “When you cast this spell, copy it for each other spell that was cast before it this turn. If the spell has any targets, you may choose new targets for any of the copies.”\n4301-\n4302:702.40b If a spell has multiple instances of storm, each triggers separately.\n4303-\n4304:702.41. Affinity\n4305-\n4306:702.41a Affinity is a static ability that functions while the spell with affinity is on the stack. “Affinity for [text]” means “This spell costs {1} less to cast for each [text] you control.”\n4307-\n4308:702.41b If a spell has multiple instances of affinity, each of them applies.\n4309-\n4310-702.42. Entwine\n4311-\n--\n7094-Adventurer Card\n7095-Cards with a two-part card frame (one part of which is inset on the left) on a single card where the alternative characteristics include the Adventure spell type. See rule 715, “Adventurer Cards.”\n7096-\n7097:Affinity\n7098:A keyword ability that reduces how much mana you need to spend to cast a spell. See rule 702.41, “Affinity.”\n7099-\n7100-Afflict\n7101-A keyword ability that makes the defending player lose life for blocking. See rule 702.130, “Afflict.”\n--\n8955-The collection of stickers found on an insert in Unfinity booster packs. See rule 123, “Stickers.”\n8956-\n8957-Storm\n8958:A keyword ability that creates copies of a spell. See rule 702.40, “Storm.”\n8959-\n8960-Stun Counter\n8961-A counter that stops a permanent from untapping. See rule 122.1d."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RaVWivbMoyZB1n31Cq7Ufj","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"f8177819-7c5f-4442-907f-c6baca59a535","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:25:05.538Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_