{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01X28FxP3XG7wtRmqcm9FsSf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E91Y4Kd8rqXpVWisXrby1G","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale for SOS 245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\n## File: cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py\n\n### TestWitherbloomProperties (10 tests)\nStatic card data validation matching the card spec.\n\n- `test_is_creature` — Verifies the class inherits from Creature.\n- `test_name` — Name matches \"Witherbloom, the Balancer\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — Mana cost is {6}{B}{G}.\n- `test_mana_value_is_eight` — CMC is 8 (6 generic + B + G).\n- `test_card_type_creature` — Has CREATURE card type.\n- `test_supertype_legendary` — Has LEGENDARY supertype.\n- `test_subtypes_elder_dragon` — Has \"Elder\" and \"Dragon\" subtypes.\n- `test_power_toughness` — 5/5 base stats.\n- `test_has_flying` — Has FLYING keyword.\n- `test_has_deathtouch` — Has DEATHTOUCH keyword.\n\n### TestWitherbloomSelfAffinity (7 tests)\nTests the card's own \"Affinity for creatures\" via `cost_reduction()`.\n\n- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction` — 0 creatures = 0 reduction.\n- `test_one_creature_reduces_by_one` — 1 creature = 1 reduction.\n- `test_three_creatures_reduces_by_three` — 3 creatures = 3 reduction.\n- `test_six_creatures_reduces_by_six` — 6 creatures fully reduces generic (6).\n- `test_opponent_creatures_do_not_count` — Only controller's creatures count.\n- `test_non_creature_permanents_do_not_count` — Enchantments etc. are excluded.\n- `test_excess_creatures_beyond_generic_cost` — cost_reduction returns raw count; clamping is the casting pipeline's job.\n\n### TestWitherbloomGrantsAffinityToInstants (7 tests)\nTests the \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" ability. Uses `get_cost_reduction` from the casting pipeline to observe the effective reduction.\n\n- `test_instant_gets_cost_reduction_from_creatures` — An instant benefits from affinity when Witherbloom is on the battlefield.\n- `test_sorcery_gets_cost_reduction_from_creatures` — A sorcery also benefits.\n- `test_creature_spell_does_not_get_affinity` — Creature spells do not receive the granted affinity.\n- `test_opponent_instant_does_not_get_affinity` — Opponent's spells are not affected.\n- `test_affinity_counts_witherbloom_itself` — Witherbloom is a creature and counts for its own granting.\n- `test_affinity_clamped_to_generic_cost` — Reduction is clamped to the spell's generic mana cost.\n- `test_no_creatures_no_reduction_for_instant` — Without Witherbloom on the battlefield, instants get no bonus.\n\n### TestWitherbloomCastingWithAffinity (2 tests)\nIntegration with the casting pipeline for Witherbloom's own cost.\n\n- `test_witherbloom_castable_with_fewer_mana_when_creatures_exist` — 3 creatures reduce generic from 6 to 3.\n- `test_witherbloom_free_generic_with_six_creatures` — 6 creatures reduce generic to 0, only {B}{G} remains.\n\n### TestWitherbloomEdgeCases (2 tests)\nBoundary and dynamic behavior tests.\n\n- `test_witherbloom_on_battlefield_counts_itself_for_own_spells` — When on the battlefield, it counts itself for granting affinity to instants/sorceries.\n- `test_multiple_witherblooms_stack_affinity_on_self` — Creature count is dynamic, not snapshotted at registration time.\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **Protection from colors**: Out of scope for this card; tested by the engine's protection tests.\n- **Deathtouch combat interaction**: Engine-level behavior tested by engine_tests.\n- **Flying blocking restrictions**: Engine-level behavior tested by engine_tests.\n- **Multiple Witherblooms (legendary rule)**: The legendary rule is an engine-level SBA, not a card-specific behavior.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6011,"cache_read_input_tokens":65084,"