{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EPmGLpkMfW1HoRsv4bsk1Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0164W7D15hUyCKosU3qEuGNZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation Rationale for sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n### Card Implementation (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n- Extends `Creature` with correct stats: {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying, Deathtouch.\n- `cost_reduction(game)` implements self-affinity by counting creatures the controller controls on the battlefield.\n- `register_triggers(game)` registers an external cost-reduction provider on the game state that grants affinity for creatures to the controller's instant and sorcery spells.\n\n### Engine Extension: External Cost Reduction Providers\nThe card's \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" ability requires the casting pipeline's `get_cost_reduction` to account for cost reductions from *other* permanents, not just the spell's own `cost_reduction()` method. Three additive engine changes support this:\n\n1. **`GameState._cost_reduction_providers`** (game_state.py): A new list attribute storing dicts with `source` (the permanent) and `provider` (a callable `(game, card, controller) -> int`). Initialized in `__init__`.\n\n2. **`get_cost_reduction` enhancement** (casting.py): After querying `card.cost_reduction(game)`, iterates over `_cost_reduction_providers` and sums their contributions. The total is still clamped to the spell's generic mana cost.\n\n3. **Cleanup on leave-battlefield** (zones.py): When a permanent leaves the battlefield, `move_to_zone` now also removes its entries from `_cost_reduction_providers`, paralleling the existing unregister calls for triggers and replacement effects.\n\n### Data Structure Choice\nUsed `list[dict]` with `source` and `provider` keys for the provider registry. This mirrors the pattern used by `TriggerManager` (source-based identity matching for unregistration) and is simple to iterate during cost computation.\n\n## Conventions Established\n- Permanents that grant cost reduction to other spells should register a provider callable via `game._cost_reduction_providers` in their `register_triggers` method. The provider callable signature is `(game, card, controller) -> int`. Cleanup is automatic when the permanent leaves the battlefield.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":151,"cache_read_input_tokens":69653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":151,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GS61Azx6HQbWwjw52LWJRE","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"6a33668b-2628-4ecd-a501-6481348f3d5a","request_id":"req_011CbUp1YyApK6KPsamghQhP","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245"}
