{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011YW3MNMEqGskdzM78bmxc4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation Rationale for sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n2\t\n3\t## Design Decisions\n4\t\n5\t### Card Implementation (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n6\t- Extends `Creature` with correct stats: {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying, Deathtouch.\n7\t- `cost_reduction(game)` implements self-affinity by counting creatures the controller controls on the battlefield.\n8\t- `register_triggers(game)` registers an external cost-reduction provider on the game state that grants affinity for creatures to the controller's instant and sorcery spells.\n9\t\n10\t### Engine Extension: External Cost Reduction Providers\n11\tThe card's \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" ability requires the casting pipeline's `get_cost_reduction` to account for cost reductions from *other* permanents, not just the spell's own `cost_reduction()` method. Three additive engine changes support this:\n12\t\n13\t1. **`GameState._cost_reduction_providers`** (game_state.py): A new list attribute storing dicts with `source` (the permanent) and `provider` (a callable `(game, card, controller) -> int`). Initialized in `__init__`.\n14\t\n15\t2. **`get_cost_reduction` enhancement** (casting.py): After querying `card.cost_reduction(game)`, iterates over `_cost_reduction_providers` and sums their contributions. The total is still clamped to the spell's generic mana cost.\n16\t\n17\t3. **Cleanup on leave-battlefield** (zones.py): When a permanent leaves the battlefield, `move_to_zone` now also removes its entries from `_cost_reduction_providers`, paralleling the existing unregister calls for triggers and replacement effects.\n18\t\n19\t### Data Structure Choice\n20\tUsed `list[dict]` with `source` and `provider` keys for the provider registry. This mirrors the pattern used by `TriggerManager` (source-based identity matching for unregistration) and is simple to iterate during cost computation.\n21\t\n22\t## Conventions Established\n23\t- Permanents that grant cost reduction to other spells should register a provider callable via `game._cost_reduction_providers` in their `register_triggers` method. The provider callable signature is `(game, card, controller) -> int`. Cleanup is automatic when the permanent leaves the battlefield.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQsQV6bKSgGXoWTWADzHzM","session_id":"1fe34661-6a3c-4b16-8a42-0f618466dfcb","uuid":"fd6885b7-f13d-4be2-aaf7-ede6b40c2f1a","timestamp":"2026-05-28T10:31:08.590Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_245 implementation"}
